{"klog.NewContext(ctx, d.Log) stores the base d.Log in the context instead of the enriched log variable that was built with name, kind, and method values, causing downstream logging to lose those fields": 0.9804508686065674, "When d.Storage.Create fails, d.recordLegacyDuration is called instead of d.recordStorageDuration, corrupting observability data by attributing storage failure to the legacy metric": 0.9848904013633728, "d.recordStorageDuration passes name (individual resource name) as the third argument instead of options.Kind, causing metrics to be bucketed by individual object names rather than resource kinds and polluting label cardinality": 0.9632725715637207, "In DeleteCollection goroutine, d.recordStorageDuration is called instead of d.recordLegacyDuration for the legacy write operation": 0.9922810196876526, "All four goroutines (Create, Delete, Update, DeleteCollection) derive their timeout context from the incoming request ctx, which may already be cancelled when the goroutine starts, causing legacy writes to fail immediately and silently": 0.9005619883537292}